[0, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2J\u001b[H\u001b[1;36m  zfsify  /  root conversion\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[38;5;245m  Ubuntu 24.04  ·  1 GiB RAM  ·  DigitalOcean  ·  existing files preserved\u001b[0m\r\n  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;37m  01  Start with a normal Ubuntu VPS\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  Existing Ubuntu installation\r\n  Filesystem      Size  Used Avail Use% Mounted on\r\n  /dev/vda1        24G  2.0G   22G   9% /\r\n  \r\n  total 129M\r\n  -rw-r--r-- 1 root root   32 Sep  7 07:08 README.txt\r\n  -rw-r--r-- 1 root root 128M Sep  7 07:08 database.bin\r\n  \r\n  Development build served from this Droplet; exact SHA256 in recording notes.\r\n  + curl -fsSL http://127.0.0.1:8765/reformat.sh\r\n  + bash\r\n  Root filesystem: /dev/vda1 on /dev/vda | used 8.50% (2115194880 / 24883167232 bytes)\u001b[31;1H\u001b[38;5;245m  Actual output · waits shortened · development build · full recording linked below\u001b[0m"]
[3, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2J\u001b[H\u001b[1;36m  zfsify  /  root conversion\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[38;5;245m  Ubuntu 24.04  ·  1 GiB RAM  ·  DigitalOcean  ·  existing files preserved\u001b[0m\r\n  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;37m  02  Review the plan before any changes\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  PRESERVE: your Ubuntu installation, users, applications and files move to ZFS.\r\n  Devices: source /dev/vda1; temporary /dev/vda32; final /dev/vda2.\r\n  /dev/vda (512 MiB ZFSBootMenu partition omitted):\r\n    [              original ext4              ]\r\n    [       smaller ext4      ][ temporary ZFS ]  shrink offline; copy + verify\r\n    [       new ZFS member    ][ temporary ZFS ]  attach mirror; resilver\r\n    [       new ZFS member    ][ free space    ]  detach temporary member\r\n    [                   ZFS                   ]  grow; / and /boot on ZFS\r\n  The server reboots into RAM. Services are offline during migration.\r\n  Original ext4 is removed only after the copy is checksum-verified.\r\n  Power loss during repartitioning can require provider recovery.\u001b[31;1H\u001b[38;5;245m  Actual output · waits shortened · development build · full recording linked below\u001b[0m"]
